{"id": "EUVD-2026-102290", "enisaUuid": "f3663767-8cf1-3557-8e73-c77d9c7abdb7", "description": "WildMIDI through 0.5.0 contains a heap out-of-bounds read vulnerability in _WM_ParseNewHmi() in src/f_hmi.c that reads past buffers when handling 0xfe sub-events. Attackers can supply a crafted HMI file placing a 0xfe 0x10 sub-event near the buffer end to read up to four bytes past the allocation, crashing the decoding application.", "datePublished": "2026-10-15T18:57:50", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T19:41:27", "baseScore": 6.8, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:L/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haind-pwn/wildmidi-hmp-chunk-length-underflow-oob-read", "https://github.com/Mindwerks/wildmidi/blob/340472ed4633d139d30c660b90eca03c1320e593/src/f_hmi.c#L268-L290", "https://github.com/Mindwerks/wildmidi", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/wildmidi-through-0.5.0-heap-out-of-bounds-read-via-wm-parsenewhmi"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-111163", "GHSA-mgqp-8p5v-r4q9"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "a7c56bc0-f398-3073-b8ad-6d34b5869bc3", "product": {"name": "WildMIDI", "vendor": {"name": "Mindwerks"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22640.5.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "ce93a01a-d49b-3aab-9fb3-7480e34f8361", "vendor": {"name": "Mindwerks"}}], "isExploited": false}